{
  "version": "0.11.3",
  "describes": "Conformance vectors that define a conforming implementation (specification, Conformance).",
  "kinds": {
    "patch": "input.lg + expected.json [+ transport.json]",
    "token": "tokens.json: a list of {valid, token}",
    "negative": "input.lg + reject.json: {stage: parse|apply}",
    "determinism": "input.lg + transport.json {repeat, permutations[{file, log}], activations, expected, log}: no expected.json (declaration order affects the static observation by construction); a runner repeats and permutes itself — verdicts and decisions MUST equal expected for every run and permutation, the log MUST equal log on every repeat and each permutation's own log, which follows the SPEC §7.4 tie-break for that declaration order (SPEC §7.5; conformance/README.md, Determinism vectors)"
